# The Conversation France. Academic authors, but edited by a newsroom to a house
# style, which puts it in a different register from the journals: shorter
# sentences, direct questions, exclamations, and the interrogative punctuation
# that formal academic prose barely contains.
#
# The French edition's feed carries some English-language articles, and English
# prose in a French corpus manufactures findings the publisher never wrote:
# `fr.apostrophe` fires on "don't" and `fr.missing-space-before-high-punctuation`
# fires on every correctly set English colon. Every URL below was checked for
# French by counting function words in the extracted text, not by trusting the
# feed, and seven English articles were dropped.
# Frozen 2026-08-10. format: html
#
# A second column is an Internet Archive capture: fixed bytes, so a rebuild
# reproduces instead of resampling. A URL without one is fetched live, and
# `--live` ignores the column entirely. gates/README.md has the coverage.
